se({\"in_flight\": gauge.value})`","Dockerfile.mcp:57 `sys.exit(0 if urllib.request.urlopen(...).status==200 else 1)` — status-only","autodeploy.sh:688 `curl -fsS -m 3 \"http://127.0.0.1:${mcp_newport}/health\" >/dev/null` — body discarded","AC says '/health reports store status' without stating it must return non-200 on missing store or that the gate must parse the body"],"finding":"The AC option '/health reports store status' does not specify that the readiness signal must be observable by the EXISTING gate, which only inspects HTTP status (Dockerfile HEALTHCHECK checks `.status==200`; autodeploy :688 does `curl -fsS ... /health >/dev/null`, discarding the body). A store-status field added to the 200 JSON body would be silently ignored, leaving a storeless container still passing.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"face4bb7700d899d1","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria, first bullet","norm_id":"n9d595acf5f250103","priority":0.8889,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Implementer adds a `store: \"absent\"` field to the 200 /health body; the existing curl/HEALTHCHECK still sees 200 and promotes the storeless container"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Have the readiness endpoint return a non-200 (e.g. 503) when a store is expected but absent, so the unchanged status-only probes catch it; if a 200-with-body design is preferred, the AC must also require updating the gate and HEALTHCHECK to parse the field.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.8889,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"high","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"high"}}},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State the fail-open/fail-closed disposition of the store-readiness gate — for the store check it must fail CLOSED (an unreadable/erroring store signal must NOT promote), which is the opposite of autodeploy's existing fail-open-on-unreadable convention for the drain check.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.0889,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["autodeploy.sh:132-133 'Unreadable fails OPEN (a broken probe must not wedge deploys)'","autodeploy.sh:553 'Fail OPEN on an unreadable signal: a bot that cannot answer /health is likely broken'","The plan's ACs do not state the fail-open/fail-closed disposition of the store-readiness check"],"finding":"The plan does not state whether the new store-readiness gate fails OPEN or CLOSED on an unreadable/erroring signal. autodeploy's established posture is fail-open on unreadable signals (a broken probe must not wedge deploys), which — if applied here — would let a storeless container that errors or returns unparseable output still promote, defeating the purpose.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f9deb35934774856f","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria (all bullets) / Why this matters","norm_id":"nc0223f6a03d18e8c","priority":0.8889,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["New /ready endpoint 500s or returns malformed JSON on a storeless container; a fail-open gate promotes it anyway"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.8889,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"uncertifiable_outcome","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"high","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"high"}}},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Correct the readiness-gate citation to point at the actual /health promotion probe (autodeploy.sh:688) rather than the MCP_HEALTH_TIMEOUT var (:130), and fix the journald citation from docker-compose.yml:383 to :409.","cohort":["G1G2"],"criteria":["G1G2"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.36,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["autodeploy.sh:130 = 'MCP_HEALTH_TIMEOUT=...readiness deadline'; the promotion probe is autodeploy.sh:688 'curl -fsS -m 3 http://127.0.0.1:${mcp_newport}/health'","docker-compose.yml journald drivers verified at lines 72, 258, 306, 409 (not 383 — line 383 is 'volumes:')"],"finding":"Two of the plan's line-number citations are imprecise: (a) autodeploy.sh:130 is labeled 'the blue-green readiness gate promotes on that same probe', but :130 is the MCP_HEALTH_TIMEOUT deadline variable — the actual /health promotion probe is the curl at autodeploy.sh:688; (b) the journald corroboration cites docker-compose.yml:72,258,306,383, but line 383 is a 'volumes:' key — the fourth journald driver is at :409.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f698c223829821a13","impact":0.44,"is_primary":null,"location":"Evidence section; 'infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh:130' and 'docker-compose.yml:72,258,306,383'","norm_id":"nfdc386876fc5c219","priority":0.44,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["An implementer following the plan navigates to autodeploy.sh:130 expecting the promotion gate and finds only a timeout var, or to docker-compose.yml:383 expecting a journald driver and finds a volumes key."],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Change 'infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh:130' to reference the promotion probe at autodeploy.sh:688 (keeping :130 only as the timeout that bounds it), and change the journald line list to '72,258,306,409'.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"na","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"incomplete_enumeration","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":null,"blocking_enabled":null,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["P6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":null,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["no verification commands or testing plan referenced"],"finding":"Acceptance-criteria / definition-of-done quality issues.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f607dd457c67f9209","impact":0.4,"is_primary":null,"location":"","norm_id":"ned06ebc801a522e3","priority":0.4,"reason":null,"recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Split compound criteria, replace subjective terms with observable outcomes, and state how each is verified.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Add a rollback/back-out plan (and/or staged enablement) for the stricter readiness gate so a mis-firing store check cannot wedge the deploy pipeline.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T12","T2","T4","T5b","T5e"],"criteria":["T12","T4"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.8,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["AC1: 'the autodeploy gate consumes it'","AC3: 'a storeless container does not pass the readiness gate'","No section addresses how to revert the gate change if the new check misbehaves, nor staged rollout of the stricter gate."],"finding":"The plan changes the blue-green readiness gate so a storeless deploy that previously passed will now fail, but it specifies no rollback/back-out path for the gate change itself. A buggy or overly-strict new readiness check could wedge the entire deploy pipeline (every deploy blocked).","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fd5816252c633c675","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria AC1 / AC3; infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh:130","norm_id":"nda7c2c03e003ed96","priority":0.0,"reason":"veto:absence-refuted","recalled":false,"scenarios":["The new readiness endpoint has a bug and reports 'no store' for a healthy container, blocking promotion of every deploy.","Operators need to ship an urgent fix but the stricter gate rejects an otherwise-serving container."],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"State that the store-aware gate lands behind a toggle/env var defaulting to the old behavior first, or document the one-line revert to the plain 200 probe.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.25,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"no","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"none","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Cite the sibling provisioning ticket as an explicit dependency (`[rebar:<C>]`) and state a default for 'store expected' so AC3 is executable if the sibling is undecided.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T12","T2","T4","T5b","T5e"],"criteria":["E2","E6"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.7057,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["AC2 references a 'sibling provisioning ticket' with no cited dependency edge (E6 taxonomy item 9).","AC3's gate assertion is gated on 'when a store is expected', a fact owned by that sibling."],"finding":"AC2 and AC3 defer the store-expected decision to 'the sibling provisioning ticket' but the plan declares no dependency edge to it. AC3's condition '(when a store is expected)' is unresolvable without knowing that sibling's decision, so the readiness semantics cannot be finalized in isolation.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"feeca72986cda00e0","impact":0.33,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria AC2 ('Whatever the store decision in the sibling provisioning ticket') and AC3 ('when a store is expected')","norm_id":"n9fa50d19e445d606","priority":0.0943,"reason":"veto:absence-refuted","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Executor cannot decide whether a storeless container SHOULD fail the gate without the sibling's provisioning decision."],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.2857,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"no","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"na","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"na","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify that the store-aware readiness check fails-closed (reports not-ready) when the store probe itself errors, and surfaces the error in the response/log.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T12","T2","T4","T5b","T5e"],"criteria":["T5b"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.8263,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["AC1 introduces a store-status read into the readiness path; no error-handling behavior is stated for the probe raising.","The whole ticket is motivated by silent log-and-continue masking failures, so the probe's own error mode is decision-relevant."],"finding":"The readiness check now reads the ticket store (a new I/O failure point), but the plan does not specify how the check behaves if the store probe itself errors (permission/IO exception) — whether it fails-closed (not ready) or fails-open (ready).","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f9722b48fca91de66","impact":0.33,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria AC1 (store-aware readiness)","norm_id":"n9ba7223274fa381e","priority":0.1237,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Store directory exists but is unreadable; the readiness probe throws — does the container count as ready or not?"],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.375,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"na","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}}],"impact_model_version":"plan-v5","material_fingerprint":"7d7c6558d26da027","material_parts":{"children":["647ea2107ca5072f",0],"description":["06563ab4758944cb",2095],"description_boxes":["0aad7da77d2ed59c",0],"file_impact":["129cf9bd4d7b9514",7],"ticket_id":["59039edcc8f15b8a",19]},"metrics":{"cache_read_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"claim_path":"no-llm/no-ne